IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`

-- Employment Insurance Regulations (SOR/96-332), Part IV: the pilot projects on the earnings a claimant may have while receiving benefits:
-- the allowable earnings of Pilot Projects No. 12 (reg 77.8) and No. 17 (reg 77.94); the deduction of 50% of earnings of Pilot Projects No. 18 (reg 77.95), No. 19 (reg 77.97) and No. 20 (reg 77.99).
-- Piece er5, LAYER 1: the law, objectively. Every `src:N` is a line of SOR-96-332.txt. The text is an unofficial rendering; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- Regs 77.8(3) and 77.94(3) are word for word the same rule; so are 77.95(3), 77.97(3) and 77.99(3), and 77.95(4), 77.97(4) and 77.99(4). Each rule stated several times in the text is stated once here
-- and cites every place; what differs between the projects (the windows, the cessation days) is a rule apiece. Rule names carry the first of the regulations that state them.
-- All five projects are spent. The adaptations of s 19(2), s 19 and s 152.18 of the Act are not amendments of another instrument: each states the amount a claimant of the project is paid or charged, so each is a rule here.
-- Relations (Hohfeld): the claimant of a project holds a claim to the larger allowable earnings or the smaller deduction; the Commission bears the correlative duty.
--
-- Fork F-reg77.8c ("ceases to have effect on D"): every cessation day in these five regs (August 6, 2011; August 4, 2012; August 1, 2015; August 6, 2016; August 11, 2018) is a Saturday, and every window of (2) begins on a Sunday and ends
-- on that Saturday, so a week is read as inside the section when its last day is on or before the cessation day. The same words in reg 77(7), where nothing is anchored to a week, are read in er5-pilot-claims
-- as the first day on which the paragraph is no longer in force.
-- Fork F-reg77.8d (rounding): s 6(2) of the Act rounds "a percentage ... of earnings or benefits" in Part I to the nearest dollar. The percentages here (40% of the rate; 50% of earnings) are the Regulations' own
-- and are not rounded, since the Regulations say nothing about rounding; applying s 6(2) would round each figure, by under one dollar.

§ `Regulations Part IV - Pilot Projects on earnings while receiving benefits`

§§ `The week and the cessation of the section (regs 77.8(4), 77.94(4), 77.95(5), 77.97(5), 77.99(5))`

-- A section that ceases to have effect on a day has effect for a week when the week's last day (its Saturday, six days after the Sunday that begins it) is on or before that day.
-- src:1465 | (4) For greater certainty, this section ceases to have effect on August 6, 2011.
-- src:1518 | (4) This section ceases to have effect on August 4, 2012.
-- src:1527 | (5) This section ceases to have effect on August 1, 2015.
-- src:1548 | (5) This section ceases to have effect on August 6, 2016.
-- src:1568 | (5) This section ceases to have effect on August 11, 2018.
@ref Employment Insurance Regulations reg 77.8(4), reg 77.94(4), reg 77.95(5), reg 77.97(5), reg 77.99(5) (src:1465) (src:1518) (src:1527) (src:1548) (src:1568)
GIVEN `the Sunday that begins the week` IS A DATE
      `the day on which the section ceases to have effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.8(4) the section has effect for the week` IF
    (`the Sunday that begins the week` PLUS 6) AT MOST `the day on which the section ceases to have effect`

§§ `Reg 77.8 - Pilot Project No. 12, increased allowable earnings`

-- src:1460 | 77.8 (1) Pilot Project No. 12 is established for the purpose of testing whether increasing the amount of a claimant’s allowable earnings from employment while the claimant is receiving benefits would encourage more claimants to accept employment while receiving benefits.
