      `the day on which the benefit period ends, if it has` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: Schedule I (piece er6)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `reg 77.8(2) the claimant is included in Pilot Project No. 12` IF
        (   `the day` `the day on which the benefit period is established` `falls within` `reg 77.8(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established or end for Pilot Project No. 12`
         OR (CONSIDER `the day on which the benefit period ends, if it has`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
             WHEN JUST ends THEN `the day` ends `falls within` `reg 77.8(2) the period in which the benefit period must be established or end for Pilot Project No. 12`))
    AND `the claimant is ordinarily resident in a region described in Schedule I`

-- (3) For the purpose of Pilot Project No. 12, s 19(2) of the Act is adapted such that the maximum allowable earnings are (a) $75, if the claimant's rate of weekly benefits is less than $188; and
-- (b) 40% of the claimant's rate of weekly benefits, if that rate is $188 or more. The same words are reg 77.94(3), for Pilot Project No. 17.
