-- The formula, once: 50% of the earnings up to 90% of the weekly figure, and 100% of the earnings above it. Readings taken (fork F-reg77.95): "the earnings that are less than or equal to 90%" are
-- the part of the earnings that does not pass the threshold, so each dollar is deducted at 50% up to the threshold and at 100% above it (the purpose clause of reg 77.95(1) reads the same way); not a rate that
-- depends on whether the whole of the earnings is above or below the threshold.
GIVEN earnings IS A NUMBER
      `the weekly figure` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `er5 reg 77.95 half of the earnings up to 90 percent of the weekly figure and all of the earnings above it` IS
    (50% TIMES (min earnings (90% TIMES `the weekly figure`))) PLUS (100% TIMES (max 0 (earnings MINUS (90% TIMES `the weekly figure`))))

-- (3) s 19 of the Act is adapted by adding after subsection (2) a subsection (2.1): the amount to be deducted under subsection (2), except for the purpose of section 13, is the total of (a) 50% of the earnings
-- that are less than or equal to 90% of the claimant's weekly insurable earnings used to establish their rate of weekly benefits, and (b) 100% of any earnings that are greater than 90% of them.
-- For the purpose of section 13 the added subsection does not govern: NOTHING, and s 19(2) of the Act (piece ei1) applies. Regs 77.97(3) and 77.99(3) say the same.
